---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import tools from '../../data/tools-manifest.json';
import retirement from '../../data/tool-retirements.json';
import '../../styles/workshop-directory.css';
const guides = (await getCollection('tools')).filter(entry => !entry.data.draft).sort((a, b) => a.data.title.localeCompare(b.data.title));
const localCount = tools.filter(tool => tool.id !== 'chat-playground').length;
const behaviour: Record<string, string> = {
  'agent-check': 'Local decision aid · no save',
  'prompt-workbench': 'Local editor · optional browser saves',
  'prompt-diff': 'Local comparison · reads saved versions',
  'json-validator': 'Local schema check · no save',
  'context-window': 'Local plan · dated model limits',
  'model-comparison': 'Local calculation · dated model rates',
  'token-cost': 'Local text estimate · no save',
  'chat-playground': 'OpenRouter request · your key · provider charges',
};
const takeaways: Record<string, string> = {
  'agent-check': 'A starting approach, the reasons and a bounded next step.',
  'prompt-workbench': 'Filled messages, an exportable request and optional saved versions.',
  'prompt-diff': 'A report of changed words, estimated tokens and input cost.',
  'json-validator': 'Exact constraint failures or a matching schema result.',
  'context-window': 'A copyable plan with context and reply-limit warnings.',
  'model-comparison': 'A CSV of workload estimates, sources and assumptions.',
  'token-cost': 'An estimate that includes repeated conversation history.',
};
const jobs = [
  { id: 'make', number: '01', verb: 'Make', title: 'Make a prompt', hint: 'Turn a rough request into something reusable.', output: 'Messages you can edit, compare and keep.', icon: '{ }', ids: ['prompt-workbench', 'prompt-diff'] },
  { id: 'check', number: '02', verb: 'Check', title: 'Check an output', hint: 'Find the gap between a response and its contract.', output: 'Errors you can locate and fix.', icon: '✓', ids: ['json-validator'] },
  { id: 'plan', number: '03', verb: 'Plan', title: 'Plan a request', hint: 'Budget the space and estimate the cost.', output: 'A plan with visible limits and assumptions.', icon: '≋', ids: ['context-window', 'model-comparison', 'token-cost'] },
  { id: 'decide', number: '04', verb: 'Decide', title: 'Choose the approach', hint: 'Work out how much autonomy the job needs.', output: 'A reasoned starting point for your task.', icon: '↳', ids: ['agent-check'] },
];
const connectedTool = tools.find(tool => tool.id === 'chat-playground')!;
---
<BaseLayout title="Tools" description="Choose a job, try a worked example and take something useful away. Eight browser tools for prompts, JSON, context, costs and agent decisions.">
  <div class="workshop-directory workshop-shell">
    <header class="directory-hero">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">THE SOFT CAT WORKBENCH</p><h1>Good questions.<br /><em>Working answers.</em></h1><p>Make a prompt, inspect an output or plan the next request. Start with the job. Leave with something you can use.</p><a class="text-link" href="#first-lap">New here? Try the worked example <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
      <aside class="directory-inventory" aria-label="What is on the workbench"><div><strong>{tools.length}</strong><span>small tools<br />with a clear job</span></div><p><span>{localCount} work without an API key</span><span>1 can call a model with your key</span></p><a href="#data-behaviour">See what leaves the page <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></aside>
    </header>

    <nav class="directory-task-map" aria-label="Choose a task">{jobs.map(job => <a class={'directory-task directory-task-' + job.id} href={'#tools-' + job.id}><span class="directory-task-top"><span>{job.number} / {job.verb.toUpperCase()}</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span><span class="directory-task-icon" aria-hidden="true">{job.icon}</span><strong>{job.title}</strong><span class="directory-task-hint">{job.hint}</span><span class="directory-task-count">{job.ids.length} {job.ids.length === 1 ? 'tool' : 'tools'} <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></span></a>)}</nav>

    <section class="directory-first-lap" id="first-lap" aria-labelledby="first-lap-heading">
      <div class="directory-lap-intro"><p class="eyebrow">A FIRST LAP / NO ACCOUNT NEEDED</p><h2 id="first-lap-heading">One invoice.<br />A checkable answer.</h2><p>A tiny extraction exercise. The source omits a due date. A useful answer keeps that gap visible.</p><div class="directory-specimen" aria-label="Worked example: a missing date stays missing"><div><span class="directory-specimen-label">SOURCE EXCERPT</span><p>Invoice INV-104 from Juniper Studio.<br />Amount due: GBP 129.50.</p><span class="directory-specimen-gap">No due date supplied</span></div><div><span class="directory-specimen-label">TARGET VALUE</span><code>"due_date": <b>null</b></code><span>An example to check, not a recorded model response.</span></div></div></div>
      <div class="directory-lap-steps"><ol><li><a href="/prompts/data-extraction"><span>01</span><div><strong>Start with the recipe</strong><p>Read the source, inspect the prompt and see the target result.</p></div><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a></li><li><a href="/lab/prompt-workbench?recipe=data-extraction"><span>02</span><div><strong>Make the prompt your own</strong><p>Open the same example as an editable draft. Nothing is saved or sent.</p></div><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a></li><li><a href="/lab/json-validator?preset=recipe-invoice"><span>03</span><div><strong>Check the matching contract</strong><p>Find deliberate structural errors, then load the matching example.</p></div><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a></li></ol><p>These steps do not call a model. The schema checks the shape. You still need to check each value and quote against the source.</p></div>
    </section>

    <section class="directory-tools" id="interactive-tools" aria-labelledby="tools-heading">
      <div class="directory-section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">PICK THE JOB</p><h2 id="tools-heading">A tool is a means.<br />Here is what you can take away.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/prompts">Browse the prompt recipes <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <div class="directory-job-list">{jobs.map(job => <section class={'directory-job directory-job-' + job.id} id={'tools-' + job.id} aria-labelledby={'heading-' + job.id}><div class="directory-job-heading"><span class="directory-job-number">{job.number}</span><h3 id={'heading-' + job.id}>{job.verb}.</h3><p>{job.output}</p></div><div class="directory-tool-grid">{job.ids.map(id => tools.find(tool => tool.id === id)!).map(tool => <article class="directory-tool"><a href={tool.href}><span class="directory-tool-icon" aria-hidden="true">{tool.icon}</span><h4>{tool.name}</h4><p>{tool.description}</p><span class="directory-tool-takeaway"><span>TAKE AWAY</span>{takeaways[tool.id]}</span><span class="directory-tool-open">Open tool <b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></span></a><p class="directory-tool-behaviour">{behaviour[tool.id]}</p></article>)}</div></section>)}</div>
      <article class="directory-connected"><div><p class="eyebrow">WHEN YOU WANT TO TRY A MODEL</p><h3>{connectedTool.name}</h3><p>{connectedTool.description}</p></div><div><p>{behaviour[connectedTool.id]}</p><a class="workshop-button" href={connectedTool.href}>Open Chat Playground <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><span>Only sends when you press Send.</span></div></article>
      <aside class="directory-data-note" id="data-behaviour"><h3>Know what leaves the page.</h3><p>Calculators, editors and validators process your input in the browser. Workbench saves only when you choose. Chat sends your messages and key to OpenRouter when you press Send. The tools show their own dated model records, which are not a promise of live availability.</p><a href="/privacy">Privacy and browser storage ↗</a></aside>
    </section>
    <section class="directory-guides" aria-labelledby="guides-heading"><div class="directory-section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">HOW THE PIECES WORK</p><h2 id="guides-heading">Guides tied to the build.</h2></div></div><div>{guides.map(entry => <a href={'/tools/' + entry.id}><span><h3>{entry.data.title}</h3><p>{entry.data.description}</p></span><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a>)}</div></section>
    <aside class="directory-curation"><p class="eyebrow">THE SHELF CHANGED</p><p>The old {retirement.entries.length}-entry external recommendation series has been retired. The three local guides were corrected against the work. Original dates and source history remain visible.</p><a class="text-link" href="/tools/review">What left, and why ↗</a></aside>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
